<span class="stab">Key findings for Morph</span>
<div class="ins ins-d">CPA collapsed from ~AED 7 to AED 34 from March — directly tied to pausing Performance Max. Restoring or rebuilding this campaign should be priority #1.</div>
<div class="ins ins-w">Dubai campaigns are 3× more expensive than Abu Dhabi. Hair Services Dubai CPA = AED 40 vs Abu Dhabi's AED 13. Needs dedicated strategy, not copy-paste.</div>
<div class="ins ins-w">Paid Search drives 39% of all sessions but has the lowest engagement rate (48%) and only 24s avg. session time — traffic is coming but not converting well. Landing page is the likely culprit.</div>
<div class="ins ins-d">91% of ad spend hits mobile users. With only 24s avg. engagement time, the mobile landing experience needs urgent review before scaling budget.</div>
<div class="ins ins-g">Organic Search is the highest-quality traffic: 71% engagement rate, 38s avg. session. SEO is working quietly — worth protecting and amplifying.</div>
<div class="ins ins-g">Paid Social has the longest avg. session time (40s) despite low volume (865 sessions). High-intent audience — underinvested channel for Dubai acquisition.</div>
<div class="ins ins-l">881 form submits recorded as a key event — this is the conversion anchor. Morph needs to map this to actual booking/revenue data to validate CPA quality.</div>
<div class="ins" style="border-left-color:var(--teal);">Audience targeting is solid: 96% female, 25–44 core demo = 66%. No changes needed — focus budget and creative, not targeting.</div>

